WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.290
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:04.097
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.097 --> 00:00:06.820
between Wendy's in Japan and the US.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.713
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.191 --> 00:00:13.027
In Japan, our Wendy's hamburgers

00:00:13.027 --> 00:00:14.550
come in four sizes:

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.413
junior, single, double, and triple.

00:00:18.413 --> 00:00:21.250
In the US, our burgers come in four sizes:

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.391
junior, Dave's single,

00:00:23.391 --> 00:00:26.699
Dave's double, and the Dave's triple.

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.143
Look at the size of this thing.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.640
In Japan, our nuggets come
in orders of five and 10.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.490
Our US nuggets come in four, six,

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.156
and 10-piece.

00:00:41.156 --> 00:00:43.435
Our Wendy's drinks come in three sizes:

00:00:43.435 --> 00:00:45.933
small, medium, and large.

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:48.170
And in the US we also
have three drink sizes,

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.800
small, medium,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.090
you've gotta be kidding me.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.452
Look at the size of this thing.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.200
This might be 40 ounces, Yuelei.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.181
Only one way to find out.

00:00:56.181 --> 00:00:57.014
Ho!

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.423
Oh, not quite 40.

00:01:00.423 --> 00:01:05.174
About 36 or 37 fluid ounces of Coca-Cola.

00:01:05.174 --> 00:01:06.660
And how big's a bladder?

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.720
This looks like more
than I would normally pee

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.570
in the morning.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:13.223
OK, let's measure our large drink.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.723
It measures exactly 500 milliliters.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.030
Our Wendy's fries come in two sizes.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.460
Small and medium.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.293
Our fries come in four sizes,

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:28.984
junior, small, medium,

00:01:28.984 --> 00:01:30.625
pew, large.

00:01:30.625 --> 00:01:32.544
Let's weigh our largest.

00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:34.083
[laughs]

00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:37.837
Roughly 180 grams.

00:01:37.837 --> 00:01:41.000
It weighs 135 grams.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.216
Japan's chili comes in two sizes,

00:01:43.216 --> 00:01:45.582
medium and large.

00:01:45.582 --> 00:01:48.190
And the US, our chili comes in two sizes,

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:49.970
small and large.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.340
Let us weigh the largest now.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.072
Including the paper cup, 430 grams.

00:01:56.072 --> 00:01:58.850
George: Let's weigh our large chili.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.565
265 grams.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.468
In Japan, a Wendy's burger USA double

00:02:06.468 --> 00:02:11.370
is 730 yen, or $6.38.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.720
Our US Dave's double goes for $5.99,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.490
or around 685 Japanese yen.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:22.040
That's a 6.16% decrease
in price in the US.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.042
Let's make it a meal.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.733
In Japan, if you're getting
your burger as a set,

00:02:25.733 --> 00:02:27.330
it includes a small fries

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.796
and a three-piece nuggets and a drink.

00:02:29.796 --> 00:02:32.329
It costs around 440 yen more.

00:02:32.329 --> 00:02:34.620
Our meals only include fries and drink.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.730
So a small Dave's double meal,

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:37.810
and I threw in a four-piece

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.135
because we don't have a three-piece,

00:02:39.135 --> 00:02:42.760
works out to $10.98.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.200
That's an 8.12% increased cost in the US.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.212
Mind you, we did get an extra nugget.

00:02:48.212 --> 00:02:49.840
Speaking of nuggets, in Japan,

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.257
10-piece nugget is 510 yen,

00:02:52.257 --> 00:02:55.250
which breaks down to 51 yen per nugget.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.850
In the US, a 10-piece nugget is $4.29,

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.620
which makes it per nugget around 43 cents.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.820
So per nugget average,

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.873
the US is paying 8.11% less.

00:03:05.873 --> 00:03:07.422
A Baconator double in Japan

00:03:07.422 --> 00:03:12.100
is 850 yen, or $7.43.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:16.725
In the US, you get that
same Baconator for $7.49,

00:03:16.725 --> 00:03:19.760
or 857 Japanese yen.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.268
So close. Only a 0.82% increase.

00:03:25.683 --> 00:03:28.500
Here is everything you can
get at the Wendy's in Japan

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.702
you cannot get in the US.

00:03:30.702 --> 00:03:32.360
And here's everything at a US Wendy's

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.950
you can't get in Japan.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.670
One thing I want to point
out is that in Japan,

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:40.070
Wendy's is known as Wendy's First Kitchen.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.530
First Kitchen is a
Japanese fast-food chain,

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.680
and it was acquired by Wendy's in 2016

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.979
and became a hybrid of Wendy's
and First Kitchen's menus.

00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:51.862
And we call them Fakkin,

00:03:51.862 --> 00:03:54.411
which is the abbreviation of First Kitchen

00:03:54.411 --> 00:03:55.650
in a Japanese way.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.808
It's like First Kitchen's "Fa"

00:03:57.808 --> 00:04:00.310
and kitchen's "ki" and "n."

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.226
And say: Fakkin.

00:04:02.226 --> 00:04:05.260
Repeat after me: Fakkin.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.040
[beep]

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.362
Got it, buddy.

00:04:08.362 --> 00:04:09.710
Very good!

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:13.080
So, here are our Japan's
exclusive burgers.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.420
So, this one is bacon mushroom melt,

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.930
and this one is just mushroom melt.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:22.550
We have Wendy's bacon egg burger.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:26.716
We also have Wendy's
cheese bacon egg burger,

00:04:26.716 --> 00:04:27.924
and this sauce,

00:04:29.224 --> 00:04:31.310
tartar sauce. Umai.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.750
Everybody's curious what this is.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.810
This one is Wild Rock.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.240
It's got no buns.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.210
It's got two beef patties.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.849
I think I should try this one.

00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:42.877
Itadakimasu.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.110
This meat itself has a good taste

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:49.968
and some kind of, like, peppery flavor,

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:52.180
but it's a little bit dry.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.592
I wouldn't get this again.

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:54.933
And last things,

00:04:54.933 --> 00:04:57.912
we have junior teriyaki burger,

00:04:57.912 --> 00:05:01.470
and we have junior teriyaki cheeseburger.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.430
The big bacon cheeseburger.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.122
The big bacon double.

00:05:06.122 --> 00:05:09.430
Look at this! Yep, one, two,
three, the big bacon triple.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:14.050
I mean, I don't know what angle
is best to look at this at.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.600
And then we got big
bacons on the fancy bread.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.460
This must be the big bacons classicses.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.450
This looks like a big bacon --

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.320
look, it's got shredded
cheese and stuff on this.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.310
Everything's bacon
something with these guys.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.490
At this point, it's just
like, how many slabs of meat

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.355
do you want on your bacon sandwich?

00:05:30.355 --> 00:05:33.088
Two things you can get at a Wendy's

00:05:33.088 --> 00:05:35.470
in the US you cannot get in Japan

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:38.770
or just the junior burger
and the junior cheeseburger.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.860
Look at this little guy. Look at this.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.859
Literally every fast-food burger place

00:05:42.859 --> 00:05:44.280
has a version of this.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.730
Chicken!

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.171
[grunts]

00:05:47.171 --> 00:05:49.340
The Asiago chicken sandwiches.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:54.335
We got the Asiago chicken
ranch classic club.

00:05:54.335 --> 00:05:57.220
I said that in the wrong
order, but you get what I mean.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.490
Probably this one.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:02.540
This is the fried Asiago club with bacon.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.006
And then there is the spicy,

00:06:05.006 --> 00:06:07.381
which I'm assuming is this one.

00:06:07.381 --> 00:06:09.463
And then they got the grilled.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.820
That's pretty good.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.460
Don't like Asiago?

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:16.830
Wendy's got you covered.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.060
So many chicken sandwiches at Wendy's

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.530
that of course are not Asiago'd.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.440
This is the grilled chicken sandwich.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.247
As you can see, it is grilled.

00:06:26.247 --> 00:06:29.117
And then we have the
grilled chicken big bacon.

00:06:29.117 --> 00:06:32.676
Man, they must've gotten some
deal on bacon for Wendy's.

00:06:32.676 --> 00:06:33.970
Everything's got bacon on it!

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:35.427
I'm going to go ahead
and assume this is the

00:06:35.427 --> 00:06:37.820
big bacon fried chicken sandwich,

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.511
'cause it has bacon on it.

00:06:39.511 --> 00:06:42.350
So you have the spicy big
bacon cheddar chicken.

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.210
In Japan, our Wendy's have pasta,

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.600
which were originally on
the First Kitchen menu.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.960
So here we have
ramen-style soy cream pasta

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:52.860
with spinach and ham.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.276
Expires 2023,

00:06:56.276 --> 00:06:58.110
January 20.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.535
Joe, I'll keep this for you.

00:07:00.535 --> 00:07:03.070
Nah, my guy, you can go
ahead and throw that out.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:07.250
And next we have ramen-style
dandan soup pasta

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.610
with spinach and ham.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:13.730
So, dandan soup is kind of like
a spicy chili-flavored soup

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:16.160
with miso and pork mince.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.630
Dandan soup and dandan ramen
are very popular in Japan.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.905
Tomato sauce pasta

00:07:22.905 --> 00:07:26.696
with mozzarella and bacon.

00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:30.973
All right, next we have beef
cheek meat cream spaghetti.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.245
Plastic.

00:07:33.245 --> 00:07:34.078
Mm.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:38.714
Next we have carbonara spaghetti.

00:07:38.714 --> 00:07:39.655
Naotomo: Carbon-AR-a.

00:07:39.655 --> 00:07:41.138
Carbon-AAH-ra.

00:07:41.138 --> 00:07:42.688
Carbona-rrra.

00:07:42.688 --> 00:07:43.793
A-rrra? OK.

00:07:43.793 --> 00:07:45.135
Carbra-rrra.

00:07:45.135 --> 00:07:46.118
[crew laughing]

00:07:46.118 --> 00:07:47.534
It's got bacon

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:51.684
and this creamy carbona-rrra sauce.

00:07:51.684 --> 00:07:53.260
Molto bene!

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:58.220
Last thing I have is
spicy cod roe spaghetti.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:02.330
So, spicy cod roe in Japanese is mentaiko,

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:06.640
and mentaiko spaghetti is
also very popular in Japan.

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.522
Unfortunately, some Americans I know

00:08:08.522 --> 00:08:10.630
don't like mentaiko so much

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.810
because of the texture and smell.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.401
But for me, mentaiko,

00:08:14.401 --> 00:08:17.960
it's super Fakkin delicious.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:21.230
Uh, it's been a while
since I got this one.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.236
It's been, like, three hours.

00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:24.411
Itadakimasu.

00:08:27.284 --> 00:08:28.234
Mm.

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:30.470
Joe, try it out.

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.761
I appreciate the offer, George,

00:08:31.761 --> 00:08:33.594
but you can go ahead and finish that,

00:08:33.594 --> 00:08:36.500
'cause it looks Fakkin disgusting.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.830
We got salads.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.196
Over here on this end, the first one

00:08:39.196 --> 00:08:42.140
looks like we got the
Parmesan Caesar salad.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.490
Comes with, of course, Caesar dressing

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.340
and what looks to be Parmesan crisps.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.640
This next salad is ridiculous.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.560
We're going to go ahead and
put quotes around salad.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:55.470
Wendy's has a taco "salad" that comes

00:08:55.470 --> 00:09:00.450
with tortilla chips, sour
cream, signature salsa,

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.560
and, if that wasn't enough, chili.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.910
And before we continue,

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.725
you confirmed that the taco salad

00:09:06.725 --> 00:09:08.340
is supposed to have chili on it?

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.340
They told you that.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.700
Just gotta get the chips all around here.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.630
I can't believe this.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.310
This is so gross.

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:17.860
Signature salsa, then chili.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:20.280
Oh, it smells so bad.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.181
Oh, God.

00:09:22.181 --> 00:09:23.014
Eh.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.500
I'm just -- this is just like eating chili

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.030
with tortilla chips.

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:27.863
They said there was some salt --

00:09:27.863 --> 00:09:29.538
I'm just pushing this s--- around.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.630
On to the next salad,

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:35.330
the Southwest avocado salad.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.800
Oh, my God, there's bacon on it!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:37.760
That's weird.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.350
That was in Dave Thomas' obituary.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.000
"I want everything to
be covered in bacon."

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:45.110
But yeah. Chicken, avocado,
bacon, cheese, and some sauce.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:45.943
This makes sense.

00:09:45.943 --> 00:09:48.209
And the last salad,

00:09:48.209 --> 00:09:49.426
apple pecan salad.

00:09:49.426 --> 00:09:50.351
That smells.

00:09:50.351 --> 00:09:52.460
Oh, 'cause it's got blue cheese on it.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.001
Roasted pecan bits.

00:09:54.001 --> 00:09:55.551
Pomegranate vinaigrette!

00:09:57.691 --> 00:09:59.040
Mm. Apples are nice.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:01.830
It's kind of nice to get a
little bit of actual fruit,

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.360
something nutritious while doing this.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.530
It's like my body's like, "What is this?!"

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:07.380
So, here are Japan's side menu.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:09.830
We have a few flavor options for fries.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:13.556
So we have happy butter flavor fries.

00:10:14.415 --> 00:10:16.420
Happy butter flavor.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.712
It has just subtle buttery flavor. Mm.

00:10:19.712 --> 00:10:23.000
Burnt butter soy sauce flavor.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.517
Rip it off. Bwah!

00:10:24.517 --> 00:10:27.510
I don't know what's going on
here, but it's pretty good.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.430
Much better than this.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:32.240
Savory steamed potato butter.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.970
It gets quite strong buttery flavor.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:36.861
Definitely I prefer this one

00:10:36.861 --> 00:10:39.028
than the happy butter flavor.

00:10:39.028 --> 00:10:40.490
This is not happy.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:44.117
This one is chicken consommé flavor.

00:10:44.117 --> 00:10:45.300
Mm.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.440
This is the best fries
I've ever had in my life.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:50.823
Now I'm going to introduce you

00:10:50.823 --> 00:10:55.422
this spicy chicken breast.

00:10:55.422 --> 00:10:57.880
Wendy's in the US also has baked potatoes.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:58.850
See what we got.

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:01.768
Of course, there's your regular.

00:11:01.768 --> 00:11:03.102
And this one, oh, yeah.

00:11:03.102 --> 00:11:05.220
This one's got, like,
chives and stuff in it.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.387
If I was to stop here, you would go,

00:11:07.387 --> 00:11:11.430
"Wow, what a tasteful
selection of healthy potatoes."

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:13.550
But of course we don't stop here.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:18.255
We move on to absolute
baked-potato madness.

00:11:18.255 --> 00:11:20.863
Ah, No. 1, oof.

00:11:20.863 --> 00:11:22.330
Cheese baked potato.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.080
Drowned this thing in cheese.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.562
It's like -- ooh!

00:11:25.562 --> 00:11:27.620
It's, like, caked to the side. Blech.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.128
Ugh. Ugh.

00:11:29.128 --> 00:11:32.447
Oh, God! [laughs]

00:11:32.447 --> 00:11:35.080
The chili and cheese baked potato.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.246
Blech.

00:11:36.246 --> 00:11:39.054
If you are like me, you're
wondering to yourself,

00:11:39.054 --> 00:11:40.510
something's missing.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:44.973
Something is missing from
this potato menu, Yuelei!

00:11:44.973 --> 00:11:46.400
Can you guess what that is?

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:49.900
The bacon cheese baked potato!

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.422
Oh, they got big pieces
of bacon on this one too.

00:11:52.422 --> 00:11:53.463
Oof!

00:11:53.463 --> 00:11:55.340
You can get spicy chicken nuggets.

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:56.639
Yessiree Bob.

00:11:57.548 --> 00:11:59.448
Seasoned potatoes.

00:11:59.448 --> 00:12:01.430
All right, so fruit finally made the menu.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:02.270
Apple slices.

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:04.300
It wouldn't be a Wendy's category

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.810
without the Baconator fries.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:09.030
We need the bacon meter in this episode.

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.611
Last of the sides.

00:12:10.611 --> 00:12:11.822
Oh, yeah.

00:12:11.822 --> 00:12:12.813
Oatmeal bar.

00:12:12.813 --> 00:12:13.930
Looks like a Clif bar.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.360
Whoa, that's actually pretty good.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:20.550
So, here are our Japan's exclusive drinks.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.717
We have tapioca royal
milk tea with brown sugar

00:12:23.717 --> 00:12:26.820
and tapioca milk with brown sugar.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:27.936
Tornado.

00:12:29.411 --> 00:12:30.477
Mm!

00:12:31.686 --> 00:12:33.352
This is amazing.

00:12:33.352 --> 00:12:34.640
Simply amazing.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.550
I love this.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:37.320
So, here are our other drinks.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:40.928
We have Pepsi, orange juice,

00:12:40.928 --> 00:12:42.600
and ginger ale,

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.433
lemonade and melon soda,

00:12:45.433 --> 00:12:48.074
peach tea and iced tea,

00:12:48.074 --> 00:12:51.710
iced matcha, and this one is iced cocoa.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:54.620
So, here we have our hot drinks.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:57.728
We have Darjeeling tea,

00:12:57.728 --> 00:13:00.211
and we have café mocha,

00:13:00.211 --> 00:13:02.546
and we have peach tea.

00:13:02.546 --> 00:13:03.862
Mm.

00:13:03.862 --> 00:13:05.030
I like this.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.080
And we have café latte

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.579
and cocoa

00:13:08.579 --> 00:13:10.780
and matcha.

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.871
This is matcha, but it looks like

00:13:12.871 --> 00:13:16.012
water from 100 years ago.

00:13:16.012 --> 00:13:18.162
Our Wendy's has Frosty-ccinos,

00:13:18.162 --> 00:13:21.512
which I'm assuming are
Frostys meet Frappuccinos?

00:13:21.512 --> 00:13:22.711
Frosty-ccinos?

00:13:22.711 --> 00:13:25.940
But it does not appear that
there's Frostys in this.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:28.944
They have two flavors,
vanilla and chocolate.

00:13:28.944 --> 00:13:31.397
I'm assuming this is the vanilla.

00:13:31.397 --> 00:13:33.594
Wendy's did smart on this
one. It isn't that sweet.

00:13:33.594 --> 00:13:36.810
I was expecting it to
be, like, undrinkable,

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:37.860
but it's actually kind of nice.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.298
All right, this one is the chocolate.

00:13:40.298 --> 00:13:41.131
Yeah.

00:13:41.131 --> 00:13:43.289
Also, it's a nice flavor.

00:13:43.289 --> 00:13:44.647
'Cause of the Frosty-ccinos,

00:13:44.647 --> 00:13:46.000
you know what that means.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.380
At Wendy's you can also get:

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.050
booyah, Frostys.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.660
They don't have these in Japan?

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:53.113
I feel like this is the staple menu item.

00:13:54.388 --> 00:13:59.313
[laughs]

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:01.883
I love these so much.

00:14:05.159 --> 00:14:08.050
Fantastic. That's fantastic.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.110
Gotta go for the chocolate.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.100
Don't bother finding me a spoon.

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.440
I'm just gonna do a little taste here.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:12.560
That's great.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:13.990
The Frostys are great.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:17.240
It's like a milkshake, but
it's super thick and delicious.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:19.532
Japan, you want this.

00:14:19.532 --> 00:14:20.440
Thick.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:21.820
It is thick!

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:25.370
In Japan, we have floats
instead of Frostys.

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.236
We have Coke float

00:14:27.236 --> 00:14:29.660
and melon soda float.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:33.070
Japan has an exclusive breakfast sandwich.

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:36.310
It's called the breakfast sandwich.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:38.690
It's got tomato, lettuce,

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:43.143
and I believe this is
beef or pork patties.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.160
OK, whereas Japan has one
exclusive breakfast sandwich,

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.643
we have way more.

00:14:48.643 --> 00:14:50.101
Like all the fast food here in America,

00:14:50.101 --> 00:14:52.340
we take our breakfast very seriously.

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:56.890
You can get yourself a
maple bacon croissant.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.690
It looks like it's a chicken sandwich

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:03.057
that of course has bacon and
maple syrup on the croissant.

00:15:03.057 --> 00:15:05.240
We have what just appears
to be the bacon biscuit.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:08.215
Bacon, egg, cheese

00:15:08.215 --> 00:15:10.865
in the incredibly dry biscuit.

00:15:10.865 --> 00:15:12.340
Bacon croissant.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.530
I don't know about this one.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:17.730
Moving on to the sausage zone
of the Wendy's breakfast.

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:20.756
This is the special sausage biscuit.

00:15:20.756 --> 00:15:23.064
No, no, no, no, no.

00:15:23.064 --> 00:15:24.180
Here's what I hate about this.

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:26.990
Pick a drier thing to have for breakfast.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.040
I feel like it'd be impossible
to swallow a bite of this.

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:30.590
You're going to choke on it.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:32.574
Here we go. See, this is
what I'm talking about.

00:15:32.574 --> 00:15:33.600
They might have gotten this backwards.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.520
This is actually the better sausage one.

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:36.990
This at least has a better chance

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.520
of not getting stuck in your throat.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.895
The sausage croissant
also has egg. Thank you.

00:15:41.895 --> 00:15:45.030
They have a few things that
are honey-butter-based.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:46.606
I am so glad that fast-food places

00:15:46.606 --> 00:15:49.220
are introducing honey
to their breakfast menu.

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:50.260
I think maybe it has to do with the fact

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.040
that chicken sandwiches
have become so popular.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.191
First one we got here is
the honey butter biscuit.

00:15:54.191 --> 00:15:55.980
[laughs]

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.220
Hey, it's just a biscuit
with honey butter.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:00.520
I mean, yeah, I'll have this anytime.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.787
I'll have this anytime.

00:16:01.787 --> 00:16:03.695
This one has some heft to it.

00:16:03.695 --> 00:16:05.526
It's the hot honey biscuit.

00:16:05.526 --> 00:16:07.784
Yeah!

00:16:08.943 --> 00:16:10.660
A little chicken on there.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:11.493
Yep.

00:16:14.352 --> 00:16:16.060
I really like that.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:19.930
This is the special chicken croissant.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:22.670
So, here are our desserts.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:25.165
So here we have Melotozzo.

00:16:25.165 --> 00:16:27.830
So, Melotozzo are
maritozzo-style pastries,

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:30.130
which are popular in
Rome and Japan as well,

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:31.930
made with melon bread.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:34.380
So melon bread is a type
of sweet Japanese bread

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:37.130
which has a sugar cookie
crust on the surface.

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.639
But what's funny is that

00:16:38.639 --> 00:16:41.732
it doesn't have a melon flavor at all.

00:16:41.732 --> 00:16:42.565
At all.

00:16:42.565 --> 00:16:44.176
The reason it's called melon bread

00:16:44.176 --> 00:16:46.380
is that it just looks like melon.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:48.440
Does it look like melon?

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:49.741
It does in Japan.

00:16:51.212 --> 00:16:52.700
Oh!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.825
And this time,

00:16:53.825 --> 00:16:57.550
First Kitchen made a
maritozzo using melon bread

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.620
and mascarpone cheese whipped cream,

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.950
and it's called Melotozzo.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:05.560
So here we have Melotozzo tiramisu

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.680
and Melotozzo matcha and Melotozzo plain.

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:12.920
So, actually, yesterday was
my birthday, February 18.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.353
Hey, it's your birthday!
Happy birthday, George!

00:17:15.353 --> 00:17:18.687
Thank you for your message!
Thank you! Arigatou gozaimasu!

00:17:18.687 --> 00:17:21.475
So this is my birthday present.

00:17:21.475 --> 00:17:24.380
All right, so let's give it a shot.

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:27.247
Best birthday present ever.

00:17:27.247 --> 00:17:28.266
Itadakimasu.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.420
This is so good.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:35.147
I can't stop eating this.

00:17:35.147 --> 00:17:36.471
Mm.

00:17:36.471 --> 00:17:39.720
So, Wendy's in Japan has a
Japanese traditional sweet

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:42.550
since it has been a
collaboration with First Kitchen.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:45.970
So we have shiratama cream zenzai.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:47.011
Ooh.

00:17:47.011 --> 00:17:50.100
So it has three main
ingredients, ice cream,

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:52.640
and sweet red beans, and the shiratama,

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.850
which is kind of like a mochi rice cake.

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:58.323
And my grandma likes this type of zenzai.

00:17:58.323 --> 00:18:00.060
This is for you, my grandma.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:03.690
And also we have mini pancakes.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.710
In the US, we only have
two exclusive desserts,

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:06.543
and they're both cookies.

00:18:06.543 --> 00:18:07.926
And that's no disrespect to cookies,

00:18:07.926 --> 00:18:09.793
cookies are great, but I want one of those

00:18:09.793 --> 00:18:12.120
fun Italian ice cream sandwiches they had.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.300
Anyway, you can get two
cookies here in the US,

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:17.750
a chocolate chunk cookie
and a sugar cookie.

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:23.837
Our Wendy's double burger is 578 calories

00:18:23.837 --> 00:18:27.170
and 29% of your daily recommended amount

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:30.920
and 60% of the recommended daily sodium.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.890
Our double burger, the Dave's
double, isn't much better.

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:36.365
Ours is 850 calories

00:18:36.365 --> 00:18:39.723
and way more fat. Over 70%!

00:18:39.723 --> 00:18:41.730
But less sodium,

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:43.760
just a bit over half of the daily amount.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.710
Still, not great.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:47.400
Make it a meal in Japan,

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:51.320
and that increases the calories to 1,089.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:56.090
That's 55% of your daily
recommended calorie intake.

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:58.380
And if you make it a combo
here, we chose the small

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:00.160
and took a few sips,

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.501
that's 440 more calories,

00:19:02.501 --> 00:19:05.559
bringing the total to 1,290,

00:19:05.559 --> 00:19:09.200
or 64.5% of your daily allowance.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:12.533
In Japan, the single menu
item with the most calories

00:19:12.533 --> 00:19:15.270
is the eight-piece fried-chicken pack,

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:20.086
which contains [gasps] 4,018 calories,

00:19:20.086 --> 00:19:23.320
201% of your daily calories.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:25.603
In the US, our single
biggest-calorie menu item

00:19:25.603 --> 00:19:27.730
is the Feed the Fam deal.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:30.255
A fam, yeah, right! This is all for you.

00:19:30.255 --> 00:19:32.400
It is two spicy chicken sandwiches,

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.120
two junior bacon cheeseburgers,

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:36.970
and four small fries.

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:39.403
Total 2,780 calories,

00:19:39.403 --> 00:19:43.980
which is 139% of your daily intake.

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:49.720
Japan's Wendy's doesn't
disclose their ingredients list.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:51.100
Why, Japan?

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.360
The US sure does.

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:55.410
Now, is there anything we
should be looking out for?

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:56.400
Of course there is.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:57.730
Let's start with sodium nitrate,

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:01.163
which is found in the Baconator's
applewood-smoked bacon.

00:20:01.163 --> 00:20:04.350
Sodium nitrate is a chemical
that is used to cure meats

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:07.500
and gives meat that appealing pink color.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:08.880
Perfect for bacon.

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:10.460
Also, get this,

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:11.860
it's super toxic.

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.860
It is restricted for purchase online.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:16.570
People have accidentally
eaten too much of it and died.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.780
It's also been used in homicides. Yikes!

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.470
Sodium nitrate is on a list

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:24.230
of Japan's designated food additives,

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:27.763
but our Wendy's gets its
bacon imported from Denmark,

00:20:27.763 --> 00:20:31.510
where it isn't banned,
but being reduced in use.

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:33.408
Our American cheese contains lecithin,

00:20:33.408 --> 00:20:35.910
a common emulsifier that,
according to one academic,

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:39.470
a worrisome number of scientific
studies have suggested

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:42.726
that too much of it
can promote depression.

00:20:42.726 --> 00:20:43.709
[sighs]

00:20:43.709 --> 00:20:45.570
The pickles contain polysorbate 80.

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:49.150
This is commonly used as
an emulsifier in foods,

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:52.220
but in pickles, it tends to
be used as a solubilizer.

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:53.810
Not how that's pronounced, sorry.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.840
Which helps other ingredients
in the brine fully dissolve.

00:20:56.840 --> 00:21:00.110
Studies have suggested it can
cause colon cancer in mice.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:01.530
Not fantastic.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.457
There is no info on Wendy's website

00:21:03.457 --> 00:21:05.470
of where the pickles come from,

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:08.720
but we want to point
out that polysorbate 80

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:11.640
is on Japan's list of
designated additives.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:15.440
And therefore, it's permitted
to be used in Japan.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:16.981
Carbra-rrra.

00:21:16.981 --> 00:21:18.681
[crew laughing]

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:22.976
Naotomo: I want to try that.

00:21:22.976 --> 00:21:24.591
[laughing]

